#### What's *CropMED?*

[CropMED]{.smallcaps} is an open dataset including areas of 191 crops (in hectares) that have been compiled and harmonized from official institutions of 48 countries in the region.

#### Which formats are available?

- **Main dataset**: [CropMED]{.smallcaps} is primarily available as a table in comma-separated values (*.csv)* format, including hectares of each crop corresponding to each administrative unit and aggregated into crop groups and subgroups (see Overview).

- **GIS extension**: [CropMED]{.smallcaps} is also available in GeoPackage format (*.gpkg*, see [definition here](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GeoPackage)) for intended usage in GIS programs.

- **Pictures**: [CropMED]{.smallcaps} also provides multiple images showing the distribution of hectares for each crop included in the dataset. These maps can be easily visualized in the `visualizer.qmd` page.

#### Scientific Article

| Please give credit to the authors by referring to the data deposit at Zenodo as follows:   
| 
| **San Segundo Molina, D., Villén Pérez, S. & Morales Castilla, I. 2026**. A harmonized fine-scale crop area dataset across administrations in Europe, the Mediterranean and the Levant. *Zenodo* [https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.2071710](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20717102 "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20717102")

#### Scientific Citation

::: callout-note
The dataset and the metadata are described from a scientific perspective in a manuscript currently under submission and review. This page will be updated to include the scientific citation as follows:

| **San-Segundo Molina, D., Villén-Pérez, S. & Morales-Castilla, I., 2026**. CropMED: A harmonized, fine-scale crop area dataset across administrations in Europe, the Mediterranean Basin and the Levant. *Journal Information To Be Completed After Publication*.
:::
